---
import '../styles/global.css';

interface Props {
  title: string;
}

const { title } = Astro.props;
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <!-- Fraunces is requested with all four axes — ital, opsz, wght, SOFT and
       WONK — so no axis is ever left to its default. Every rule that sets
       Fraunces states all four explicitly.
       Montserrat carries only 300/400/500: those are the only three weights
       any rule in src/ asks for, and body sets font-synthesis-weight: none, so
       an unused weight is pure download. -->
  <link
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght,SOFT,WONK@0,9..144,100..900,0..100,0..1;1,9..144,100..900,0..100,0..1&family=Montserrat:wght@300;400;500&display=swap"
    rel="stylesheet"
  />

  <!-- THE ENTRY-ANIMATION PATTERN'S SWITCH (R17).

       CONTEXT.md permits scroll-driven motion on this page only on one
       condition: "The finished state is the CSS default. JavaScript applies
       the animated state on load. Never the reverse." This one line IS that
       mechanism, and it is the only thing it does.

       Every motion rule on the page is scoped under html.js-motion. With no
       JavaScript there is no class, no rule matches, and the page renders
       finished -- which is what makes a screenshot capture, a client-generated
       PDF and a failed script all correct rather than blank or half-scrubbed.

       IT IS NOT A LISTENER. R12's folio owns the page's one and only scroll
       listener and a second one MUST NOT be added; this adds a class and
       returns. R17's scrub is CSS scroll-driven animation and involves no
       JavaScript at all beyond this switch.

       IN <head>, INLINE, AND SYNCHRONOUS, so the class lands before first
       paint. Deferred or at the end of <body> it would paint the finished
       pivot and then snap it to its start scale -- a flash of the finished
       state, which is the failure the pattern exists to prevent, arriving
       from the other direction. -->
  <script is:inline>document.documentElement.classList.add('js-motion');</script>
</head>
<body>
  <!-- ACCESSIBILITY AUDIT (2.4.1). The first focusable element on every
       page; visually hidden until focused (global.css, .skip-link). -->
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>
  <slot />

  <!-- Grain sits last and is a SIBLING of the content, never an ancestor —
       an ancestor carrying mix-blend-mode would trap the hero submark's own
       multiply and the white JPEG field would return. -->
  <div class="grain fixed inset-0 z-[60] pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</body>
</html>
